factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The reel_script says the 7-year-broken Narasampathi canal section and 'உபரிநீர் செல்ல சிறப்புத் திட்டம்' are mentioned, but the headline and slides say '8 ஆண்டு' / '8 ஆண்டாக' while the article says the breach has existed for 7 years; the '8 years of neglect' framing is not a figure stated for the breach.
  The reel_script states the canal 'உடைந்து கிடக்கிறது' for 7 years and that the water goes to Chithirai Savadi anicut and then into Selvasinthamani lake, but it omits that the water flow was described as the canal being built to carry Marudhamalai water directly to Noyyal, which is partially covered.
  The reel_script says the canal was built to carry rainwater from Marudhamalai directly to Noyyal, but the article says this is the canal's purpose; the reel_script's claim that the broken canal is 'இப்போது சாக்கடையாக காட்சியளிக்கிறது' attributes the current state to the canal in general, which the article attributes to lack of maintenance.
  The slides_spec 'ஏன் வெள்ளம்?' slide says the breach means water goes to the lake, but the article attributes the cause to the narrow outflow canal from the lake as well; the slide mixes two causes into one framing.
  The reel_script omits the key fact that Narasampathi is only 70% full, and omits the expert Manikandan's statement that the lake can only hold a certain amount of water and that the canal was built to handle flash-flood water.
